<title>INDIA: India's IDBI 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's IDBI 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		   11,440    vs  10,070</p>
<p>    Operating income	   57,720    vs  48,060</p>
<p>    Dividend (in rupees)	    3.5  vs	 3.0</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)		  16.76 vs	15.76</p>
<p>    Disbursals		  114,350    vs 106,930</p>
<p>    Sanctions		   170,490    vs 177,960</p>
<p>    Capital gains		   530    vs     450</p>
<p>    Other income		  1,390    vs   1,120</p>
<p>    Interest		     41,680    vs  34,000</p>
<p>    Other expenditure	   1,630    vs   1,680</p>
<p>    Gross Profit		 16,630    vs  13,950</p>
<p>    Depreciation		  1,510    vs     850</p>
<p>    Taxation			4,010    vs   3,550</p>
<p>    Income tax provision	  250    vs     520</p>
<p>written back</p>
<p>    Lease equalisation for	380    vs     --</p>
<p>earlier years  </p>
<p>Note: Term lender the Industrial &amp; Development Bank of India said the results were audited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
